{
  "version": 3,
  "note": "Locale-NEUTRAL. The jar shows pictures and the ritual counts them, so no per-locale word bank exists — the only spoken content is bare numerals. Season keys come from SEASONAL_KEYS in frontend/lib/seasonal-hub.ts; only the UNIVERSAL five are used (christmas/easter/winter/spring/summer), because 4th_of_july and thanksgivinng are en-only there and these objects are not culture-bound. Autumn has no theme key in the library at all, so acorns/pinecones/leaves ship season-null rather than mis-tagged. v3 expands the repertoire from 11 to 122 fillings, curated per-CARD (not per-theme) from the 1,495 pww-index cards that exist in all 11 locales. 122 is the honest ceiling of the CURRENT artwork, not a target: ~230 candidates are vertebrates, ~150 are people/occupations/emotions/colours, and the largest remaining pools are furniture-scale or textile. Growing past this needs new art (buttons, marbles, beads, coins, bottle caps), not a looser filter.",
  "packNote": "v3. `pack` is load-bearing rather than decorative. The jar draws exactly N real objects, so the pile height IS the quantity — which means objects must be sized by the INK inside the sprite, not by the sprite canvas. Every canvas is square; measured ink coverage across the 122 sets spans 8.2x (0.089 to 0.730), so one global size would make a jar of one filling read many times fuller than another at the SAME N — the exact dishonesty this rebuild removes, reintroduced one layer down. r70 = radius (fraction of canvas) of the disc about the alpha centroid holding 70% of the alpha mass: the PACKING radius, which deliberately discounts thin appendages (a cherry stem, a lollipop stick) because those should be allowed to overlap a neighbour. cx/cy = the alpha centroid; objects draw at -S*cx,-S*cy so the visual mass lands on the packed point. NOTE cx was omitted at v2 because the original eleven sets sat in 0.484-0.523; the 122-set library measures 0.401-0.567, which is up to 20% of a packing radius off-centre, so the term is now carried. rotMax = rotation half-range in degrees: the sprites carry BAKED directional light, so free rotation lights the pile from every direction at once and reads as stickers; radially symmetric sets tolerate 40. GENERATED BY scripts/measure-jar-sprites.js — do not hand-edit; verify-estimation-jar.js re-derives these from the sprites and fails on disagreement.",
  "freeMax": 30,
  "premiumMax": 200,
  "capacityNote": "The JAR NEVER CHANGES SIZE between capacities — the OBJECTS do. A 30-jar has big objects, a 200-jar has small ones. Three physically different glasses would destroy cross-session comparison: a child cannot tell whether today's jar holds more than yesterday's if the glass itself changed. Capacity is the teacher's choice and it drives the object size, the pile height and the number line's range — never the subscription tier, which is what the v1 tool did.",
